From 9a56000952471d096dcea564335ad98eee50a951 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vortiago <atle@havso.net>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:00:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] server: per-request generate step timings in timings (gen_*)

Each generate step sets marks at fixed points of the server loop; a mark
adds the time since the previous one to one part, so the parts sum to the
wall time from the first generated token to the last emit. Parts: gap,
prep, yield, draft, ckpt, decode, sync, spec, sample, emit. With
GGML_OP_STATS=1, gen_decode_wait_ms adds the scheduler sync and gate
wait inside the decode (from the core/0048 counters).

About 12 ggml_time_us() reads per step, always on. Clock reads only, so
the output does not change. Marks for shared parts are applied after
yield_to_queue() returns, on the main thread.

test-server-gentrace checks the accounting and the JSON fields.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6MCJC4HTKxvuGjKjqDuqQ
